#decision("Original generic circuits instead of commercial schematics")[
*Options:* model a commercial product from its service manual, or design original circuits with the same topologies. *Choice:* original circuits: a supply with a zener regulator and a 250 V tube supply, a 12AX7 tube stage, a passive bass-and-treble tone stack, an op-amp stage and a two-transistor line driver. *Why:* no copying of service documents, full ground truth, and the standard topologies of preamplifier and line-level gear. *Consequence:* transfer to real units must be shown, first on a low-voltage fault board of the driver block (T7), then by transcribing one documented product in M2.
]

<< part(3, "Objectives and measurable success criteria") >>

*Objectives.* (O1) Name the failed part or its ambiguity group accurately. (O2) Use less measurement effort than scripted troubleshooting. (O3) Be honest: calibrated probabilities, visible ambiguity groups, an explicit "no single fault fits" outcome. (O4) Be safe: no unsafe step and no invented reading. (O5) Be practical: fast, cheap, usable with plain-language complaints and meter photos. Targets T1-T7 test O1, T8-T11 O2, T12-T14 O3, T15-T17 O4 and T18-T21 O5.

*Effort units.* Effort counts << num(m('library.design.cost_dc'), 0) >> for a DC reading, << num(m('library.design.cost_scope'), 0) >> for an oscilloscope measurement, << num(m('library.design.cost_hv_extra'), 0) >> extra at a point that can exceed 50 V normally or under a fault (hands-off measurement takes longer) and << num(m('library.design.cost_lift'), 0) >> for unsoldering a part to test it, within a budget of << num(m('library.design.budget'), 0) >> per diagnosis. The weights are estimates: every effort comparison is repeated with the scope, unsoldering and high-voltage weights halved and doubled, and M2 will time them on the fault board.

